{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Hecke.TauStructureConstants","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Hecke.TauStructureConstants","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Hecke.TauSymmetrizing"],"declarations":12,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.TwBasis.tauGram_symm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.TwBasis.tauGram_symm","kind":"theorem","line":285,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/TauStructureConstants.lean#L285-L288","doc":"The Gram matrix of `τ` is symmetric — the matrix form of `tau_mul_comm`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.TwBasis.tau_mul_comm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.TwBasis.tau_mul_comm","kind":"theorem","line":267,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/TauStructureConstants.lean#L267-L283","doc":"**`τ(x y) = τ(y x)`.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.TwBasis.tauGram_det_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.TwBasis.tauGram_det_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":252,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/TauStructureConstants.lean#L252-L257","doc":"**`H_n(q)` is a symmetric Frobenius algebra for every `q ≠ 0`.**\n\nNot semisimplicity — that fails at roots of unity.  See the module\ndocstring. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.TwBasis.tauGram_det","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.TwBasis.tauGram_det","kind":"theorem","line":245,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/TauStructureConstants.lean#L245-L250","doc":"**`det` of the `τ`-Gram matrix**, with no hypothesis. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.TwBasis.tau_Tw_mul_Tw","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.TwBasis.tau_Tw_mul_Tw","kind":"theorem","line":234,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/TauStructureConstants.lean#L234-L241","doc":"**`τ(T_v · T_w) = δ_{w, v⁻¹} · q^{ℓ(v)}`** — Geck–Pfeiffer §8.1.\n\n`Ref: [geckpfeiffer2000]`.  Proved by induction on `ℓ(v)` with an arbitrary\nleft descent; no exchange condition is used.  See the module docstring. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.TwBasis.Tw_simple'_mul_self","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.TwBasis.Tw_simple'_mul_self","kind":"theorem","line":142,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/TauStructureConstants.lean#L142-L147","doc":"`T_s² = (q-1) T_s + q`, phrased at Mathlib's simple reflection. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.TwBasis.Tw_simple_mul_of_isRightDescent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.TwBasis.Tw_simple_mul_of_isRightDescent","kind":"theorem","line":125,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/TauStructureConstants.lean#L125-L140","doc":"**At a right descent, `T_w = T_s · T_{w s}`.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.TwBasis.Tw_simple_mul_of_not_isRightDescent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.TwBasis.Tw_simple_mul_of_not_isRightDescent","kind":"theorem","line":116,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/TauStructureConstants.lean#L116-L123","doc":"**At an ascent, `T_s · T_w = T_{w s}`.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.TwBasis.Tw_mul_simple_of_isLeftDescent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.TwBasis.Tw_mul_simple_of_isLeftDescent","kind":"theorem","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/TauStructureConstants.lean#L97-L114","doc":"**At a left descent, `T_v = T_{s v} · T_s`.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.TwBasis.Tw_simple_mul_self","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.TwBasis.Tw_simple_mul_self","kind":"theorem","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/TauStructureConstants.lean#L81-L93","doc":"**The quadratic relation on the basis**: `T_s² = (q-1) T_s + q`.\n\nThis is `σ_mul_Tw` at `v = s_i`, which lands in the *down* case because\n`s_i` inverts the pair `(i, i+1)` by construction. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.TwBasis.Tw_simple","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.TwBasis.Tw_simple","kind":"theorem","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/TauStructureConstants.lean#L75-L79","doc":"`T_{s_i} = σ_i`: the basis element at a simple reflection is the generator. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.TwBasis.permCoxeterSystem_simple","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.TwBasis.permCoxeterSystem_simple","kind":"theorem","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/TauStructureConstants.lean#L68-L73","doc":"Mathlib's abstract simple reflection is this corpus's adjacent\ntransposition. ","signatureChunk":0}]}